    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Shakespeare returns for his preventive visit at 51, three weeks after starting propranolol and two weeks after a cold that cleared within a week without antibiotics. He completed the health risk questionnaire beforehand. His hand is steadier and he can write a page before the script tires; he has had no dizziness, wheeze, or cold hands. He drinks about 10 standard drinks a week, no more than three on any day, and has cut coffee to two cups. He has started using a heavier pen. He has never had colorectal cancer screening. He mentioned that he is putting his affairs in order and preparing a will, and asked to talk about his wishes for medical care at the same time. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Preventive health visit, age 51</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Essential tremor on propranolol; hazardous drinking, now within agreed limits</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Propranolol extended-release 60 mg; no other medicines or supplements</td></tr><tr><td>Screening history</td><td>No colorectal screening; HIV and hepatitis C tests negative in his forties; hepatitis B vaccine series completed in his thirties</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Married; adult children nearby; a wide circle of fellow writers and friends; no financial worries</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; about 10 standard drinks a week since the brief intervention; two cups of coffee a day; walks most days; rich diet</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke detectors working; no firearms; uses a mug with a lid for hot drinks</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>Monogamous; no new partners</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Hears well; reading glasses; eye examination two years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven hours a night</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Infections</td><td>One cold this winter; no pneumonia or hospital stays</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

